00:40:56.710 --> 00:40:59.050
Shapiro wasn't kidding with that Siamese twins crack.

00:41:00.060 --> 00:41:01.200
She rented a little apartment.

00:41:01.750 --> 00:41:03.170
as Mrs. Charles Haskell.

00:41:04.280 --> 00:41:07.180
When I objected to this, she explained that it was on account of the car.

00:41:07.830 --> 00:41:11.470
The dealer might think something was funny if he called and found we were using different names.

00:41:17.110 --> 00:41:18.070
Home, sweet home.

00:41:18.390 --> 00:41:18.610
Yeah.

00:41:19.730 --> 00:41:20.490
Not bad either.

00:41:28.790 --> 00:41:29.950
Okay, so there's an idea in your mind.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:30.800
I'll take the bedroom.

00:41:31.590 --> 00:41:31.810
Yeah.

00:41:33.860 --> 00:41:34.860
Sure is stuffy in here.

00:41:43.430 --> 00:41:44.110
the windows shut.

00:41:44.550 --> 00:41:44.770
Okay.

00:41:47.270 --> 00:41:50.590
The old crow downstairs said there's a folding bed behind this door.

00:41:56.840 --> 00:41:57.660
You know how to work it.

00:42:01.750 --> 00:42:02.490
I invented it.

00:42:06.940 --> 00:42:07.560
Some joint.

00:42:07.780 --> 00:42:08.680
One can't have everything.

00:42:14.130 --> 00:42:15.150
I'm first in the bathtub.

00:42:16.540 --> 00:42:17.280
I don't know why.

00:42:17.910 --> 00:42:18.910
But I figured you would be.

00:42:29.530 --> 00:42:29.970
I'll go.

00:42:30.060 --> 00:42:40.150
it sure feels good to be clean again i must be 10 pounds lighter he must be well hitching rides

00:42:40.150 --> 00:42:47.900
isn't exactly the way you keep your school girl complexion i wish that guy with the

00:42:47.900 --> 00:42:57.990
sacks would give up nurse forget it have a drink

00:43:00.020 --> 00:43:01.020
I'm afraid I might take you up on it.

00:43:03.540 --> 00:43:05.160
If I didn't want to give you a drink, I wouldn't have offered it.

00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:08.080
Why be a sawhead, Roberts?

00:43:08.820 --> 00:43:10.020
You got yourself into this thing.

00:43:11.350 --> 00:43:13.010
You should be grateful I'm not turning you in.

00:43:14.200 --> 00:43:16.480
Why, if I wasn't regular, you'd be in the pen this minute,

00:43:16.580 --> 00:43:19.000
being photographed, fingerprinted, and being pushed around by the cops.

00:43:20.470 --> 00:43:21.170
So cheer up.

00:43:21.500 --> 00:43:22.760
Get rid of that long puss.

00:43:25.210 --> 00:43:26.830
Or is your conscience bothering you?

00:43:30.120 --> 00:43:30.480
Don't move.

00:43:33.800 --> 00:43:34.280
It isn't.

00:43:34.880 --> 00:43:36.480
Well, that's the spirit.

00:43:38.310 --> 00:43:40.250
He's dead, no moment around, I'll bring him back.

00:43:45.000 --> 00:43:47.640
I never could understand this worrying about something that's over and done with.

00:43:47.700 --> 00:43:49.420
Now, look, Vera, for the last time, I didn't kill him.

00:43:49.800 --> 00:43:50.920
Haskell was a sick man.

00:43:51.370 --> 00:43:53.230
Maybe he was dead before he fell out of the car. I don't know.

00:43:53.730 --> 00:43:55.550
Sure, sure. He died of old age.

00:43:56.650 --> 00:43:57.210
All right.

00:43:58.730 --> 00:43:59.890
So we're making a sociable.

00:44:01.850 --> 00:44:02.950
You didn't kill him.

00:44:13.910 --> 00:44:14.110
Thanks.

00:44:26.070 --> 00:44:26.630
Take care, Roberts.

00:44:27.800 --> 00:44:28.080
Yeah.

00:44:29.340 --> 00:44:29.840
Too bad.

00:44:30.250 --> 00:44:31.810
I felt like getting tight tonight.

00:44:32.490 --> 00:44:33.330
Well, I...

00:44:33.480 --> 00:44:34.260
I think you succeeded.

00:44:34.600 --> 00:44:35.280
Am I time?

00:44:36.200 --> 00:44:37.420
There's a prima donna's corset.

00:44:37.800 --> 00:44:38.420
That's good.

00:44:39.300 --> 00:44:40.340
I wanted to get tight.

00:44:41.130 --> 00:44:41.370
Bye.

00:44:41.990 --> 00:44:43.110
What have you got to get tied about?

00:44:43.820 --> 00:44:44.560
Oh, I don't know.

00:44:45.380 --> 00:44:45.940
few things.

00:44:47.270 --> 00:44:47.430
Hmm.

00:44:49.580 --> 00:44:50.680
You should have my worries.

00:44:51.340 --> 00:44:53.240
If I had your troubles, I'd stay sober.

00:44:53.740 --> 00:44:54.920
And I've got the key to that door.

00:45:00.890 --> 00:45:01.490
Maybe you're right.

00:45:01.780 --> 00:45:02.660
I'm always right.

00:45:04.790 --> 00:45:06.590
You know, I don't like your attitude, Roberts.

00:45:07.480 --> 00:45:08.860
Well, there's a lot of things I don't like.

00:45:10.420 --> 00:45:10.680
Sure.

00:45:14.390 --> 00:45:15.510
Life's like a ball game.

00:45:16.410 --> 00:45:20.190
You gotta take a swing at whatever comes along before you wake up and find it's the ninth inning.

00:45:21.460 --> 00:45:22.160
He read that song.

00:45:22.360 --> 00:45:23.460
That's a kill, Roberts.

00:45:23.830 --> 00:45:25.050
All you do is bellyache.

00:45:26.140 --> 00:45:27.060
Ignatizian.

00:45:27.610 --> 00:45:29.030
We're trying to make the better things.

00:45:30.470 --> 00:45:32.170
Maybe that's what's wrong with the whole world.

00:45:32.900 --> 00:45:33.660
Get the professor.

00:45:34.570 --> 00:45:36.970
People knock themselves out trying to buck fate.

00:45:37.200 --> 00:45:38.200
Now take you for instance.

00:45:38.600 --> 00:45:39.840
You're lucky to be alive.

00:45:40.490 --> 00:45:42.390
Well, I suppose Haskell had put up in your door.

00:45:42.760 --> 00:45:44.040
You'll be playing a harp now.

00:45:44.620 --> 00:45:45.100
Think of that.

00:45:47.110 --> 00:45:47.630
You think of it.

00:45:48.900 --> 00:45:49.420
tired of thinking.

00:45:50.570 --> 00:45:50.870
There's.

00:45:51.210 --> 00:45:52.790
Plenty of people die in this minute.

00:45:53.510 --> 00:45:55.450
I would give anything to trade places with you.

00:45:58.090 --> 00:45:59.150
I know what I'm talking about.

00:46:00.730 --> 00:46:01.370
I'm not so sure.

00:46:02.200 --> 00:46:02.500
At least.

00:46:02.870 --> 00:46:03.870
They know they're done for.

00:46:04.470 --> 00:46:05.290
They don't have to sweat blood.

00:46:05.780 --> 00:46:06.720
Wondering if they are.

00:46:08.340 --> 00:46:09.940
Your philosophy stinks, pal.

00:46:11.770 --> 00:46:13.270
We all know we're going to kick off someday.

00:46:14.010 --> 00:46:15.210
It's only a question of when.

00:46:17.110 --> 00:46:18.090
Thank you.

00:46:18.130 --> 00:46:19.390
What's got us on this subject anyway?

00:46:20.220 --> 00:46:21.700
We'll be discussing politics next.

00:46:22.940 --> 00:46:23.180
Yeah.

00:46:25.750 --> 00:46:26.330
Roger, hide the butts.

00:46:27.900 --> 00:46:28.940
On the table, sucker.

00:46:37.350 --> 00:46:40.010
We bored each other with conversation for a couple of hours longer.

00:46:40.870 --> 00:46:45.210
Every five minutes, one of us was wishing we had another bottle or a radio or something to read.

00:46:47.400 --> 00:46:48.560
And finally, we ran out of chat.

00:46:50.020 --> 00:46:53.220
I know it's only 11 o'clock, but I want to get up early and make the rounds of the used car lots.

00:46:53.700 --> 00:46:54.600
Don't worry about that.

00:46:55.370 --> 00:46:56.350
We've got all the time in the world.

00:46:56.770 --> 00:46:59.730
Maybe you have, but if you think I want to stay cooped up in this place any longer, then I have to.

00:47:00.060 --> 00:47:01.460
It's not a bad place.

00:47:01.880 --> 00:47:03.640
You pay plenty for diggings like this in New York.

00:47:03.990 --> 00:47:05.210
I wouldn't like it if it was the Ritz.

00:47:05.840 --> 00:47:11.040
You brought me liquor.

00:47:11.220 --> 00:47:12.690
You got a mean cough.

00:47:12.810 --> 00:47:13.790
I ought to do something about it.

00:47:14.550 --> 00:47:15.310
I'll be all right.

00:47:15.970 --> 00:47:16.850
That's what Camille said.

00:47:24.770 --> 00:47:26.170
Is that the dame that died of consumption?

00:47:26.490 --> 00:47:26.590
Yeah.

00:47:28.330 --> 00:47:29.970
Wouldn't it be a break for you if I did kick off?

00:47:31.020 --> 00:47:33.000
He'd be free with all Haskell's dough and car.

00:47:34.120 --> 00:47:35.140
I don't want to see anybody die.

00:47:36.840 --> 00:47:37.500
Not even me.

00:47:38.630 --> 00:47:39.390
Especially not you.

00:47:39.940 --> 00:47:40.940
One person died of me.

00:47:41.740 --> 00:47:42.140
If you did.

00:47:43.050 --> 00:47:43.870
That's all I need.

00:47:45.990 --> 00:47:47.270
You don't like me, do you, Roberts?

00:47:49.640 --> 00:47:50.000
like you.

00:47:52.070 --> 00:47:52.650
I love you.

00:47:54.630 --> 00:47:56.170
My favorite sport is being kept prisoner.

00:47:57.640 --> 00:47:59.880
After we sell the car, you can go to Blazers for all I care.

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:00.820
But not until then.

00:48:00.980 --> 00:48:08.890
I'm going to bed.

00:48:18.390 --> 00:48:19.050
Good night, Roberts.

00:48:19.570 --> 00:48:21.150
Don't try and sneak away during the night.

00:48:21.370 --> 00:48:22.290
All the doors are locked.

00:48:22.900 --> 00:48:24.600
Anyway, if I find you gone in the morning,

00:48:24.800 --> 00:48:25.960
I'll notify the police.

00:48:26.300 --> 00:48:27.080
They'll pick you up.

00:48:27.120 --> 00:48:28.500
Don't worry, I know when I'm in a spot.

00:48:30.250 --> 00:48:33.700
Well, good night. I hope that portable rack isn't too uncomfortable for you.

00:48:34.140 --> 00:48:35.600
Don't lose any sleep over it, will you?

00:49:08.600 --> 00:49:10.000
Hello?

00:49:31.340 --> 00:49:31.640
Hello.

00:49:43.660 --> 00:49:46.560
Not yet tomorrow.

00:49:53.620 --> 00:49:58.410
If this were fiction, I would fall in love with Vera, marry her and make a respectable woman of her,

00:49:58.620 --> 00:49:59.960
or else she'd make some supreme...

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:02.510
Class A sacrifice for me to die.

00:50:04.140 --> 00:50:06.180
Sue and I would bawl a little over her grave

00:50:06.180 --> 00:50:08.650
and make some crack about there's good in all of us.

00:50:09.580 --> 00:50:13.100
But Vera, unfortunately, was just as rotten in the morning

00:50:13.100 --> 00:50:14.320
as she'd been the night before.

00:50:16.590 --> 00:50:18.290
All right, all right, I'm coming.

00:50:18.490 --> 00:50:19.870
Look, Vera, it's almost noon.

00:50:21.690 --> 00:50:23.940
So what? The dealers will be there all day?

00:50:24.120 --> 00:50:26.080
They'll be there all year, too, but they'll wait that long.

00:50:26.520 --> 00:50:27.940
Shut up. You make us like a husband.

00:50:31.530 --> 00:50:33.120
Do I rate a whistle?

00:50:33.280 --> 00:50:34.500
You sure do, but let's go.

00:50:35.150 --> 00:50:36.170
Let's go, let's go.

00:50:36.290 --> 00:50:38.550
I spend 85 bucks in two hours preparing bait,

00:50:38.650 --> 00:50:39.990
and all you can say is, let's go.

00:50:40.490 --> 00:50:42.650
Come on.

00:50:48.260 --> 00:50:50.620
We passed a few used car lots last night down this way.

00:50:50.930 --> 00:50:52.230
What do you think we can get for this heap?

00:50:52.600 --> 00:50:53.720
I don't know. Plenty.

00:50:54.130 --> 00:50:55.150
Just let me handle everything.

00:50:56.250 --> 00:50:57.230
Think we can get $2,000?

00:50:57.860 --> 00:50:59.020
I don't know, but don't worry.

00:50:59.370 --> 00:50:59.970
I'll squeeze as much as...

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:01.140
Watch out of this guy as I can.

00:51:01.750 --> 00:51:03.150
I'll let it go cheap without a fight.

00:51:03.290 --> 00:51:04.410
He might think we've stolen the car.

00:51:05.200 --> 00:51:07.930
And listen, don't make any slips and call me Roberts.

00:51:08.220 --> 00:51:08.940
That'll cook us.

00:51:09.360 --> 00:51:10.780
I don't need you to tell me that.

00:51:10.980 --> 00:51:13.110
You better just sit by and keep your mouth closed.

00:51:13.750 --> 00:51:15.690
Remember, we're both in the soup if anything happens.

00:51:15.830 --> 00:51:16.630
Forget it and drive.

00:51:17.230 --> 00:51:18.950
You're my wife, Farrah Haskell.

00:51:19.950 --> 00:51:21.880
Look, after the deal's closed,

00:51:22.020 --> 00:51:23.700
let's go back to that place on Hollywood Boulevard,

00:51:23.940 --> 00:51:25.020
where I saw the fur jacket.

00:51:25.660 --> 00:51:26.220
I want to buy it.

00:51:26.680 --> 00:51:28.880
After the deal's closed, I'm saying goodbye to you.

00:51:29.630 --> 00:51:29.970
That's right.

00:51:30.640 --> 00:51:32.650
I guess I'm getting kind of used to you.

00:51:34.310 --> 00:51:35.930
Well, that's a habit you can start breaking.

00:51:36.580 --> 00:51:37.960
Let's try this place in the middle of the block.

00:51:45.200 --> 00:51:46.640
Good afternoon. What can I do for you?

00:51:46.960 --> 00:51:48.440
We're interested in selling a car.

00:51:48.600 --> 00:51:49.600
If the price is right.

00:51:52.940 --> 00:51:54.520
Well, if it's in good mechanical condition,

00:51:54.680 --> 00:51:56.550
it should blue book for about $1,600.

00:51:57.950 --> 00:51:58.990
Tony, take a look at this motor.

00:51:59.480 --> 00:51:59.960
$1,600.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:01.420
1800. Are you kidding?

00:52:13.100 --> 00:52:14.220
Well, maybe 1850.

00:52:14.940 --> 00:52:17.880
Before I let it go for 1850, I'll wreck it and collect the insurance first.

00:52:22.990 --> 00:52:24.330
This motor's seen a lot of driving.

00:52:31.400 --> 00:52:34.220
While the mechanic inspected the car, we haggled.

00:52:35.220 --> 00:52:37.700
At last, when we were all worn out, we hit a compromise.

00:52:38.550 --> 00:52:39.230
His price.

00:52:43.470 --> 00:52:44.110
Kay, it's a deal.

00:52:44.540 --> 00:52:45.780
All right, come on, we'll sign the papers.

00:52:45.980 --> 00:52:47.480
I have the ownership papers right here with me.

00:52:48.110 --> 00:52:50.350
Look, Vera, in the meantime, will you clean a dash compartment?

00:52:50.600 --> 00:52:51.700
There may be some stuff in it.

00:52:51.970 --> 00:52:53.070
All right, darling.

00:52:56.060 --> 00:52:57.820
Eighteen hundred and fifty bucks.

00:52:58.040 --> 00:52:59.220
That dirty crook...

00:53:07.160 --> 00:53:07.880
New York, huh?

00:53:08.330 --> 00:53:08.430
Yeah.

00:53:08.970 --> 00:53:10.390
But you bought the car in Miami.

00:53:10.780 --> 00:53:10.980
Yeah.

00:53:12.350 --> 00:53:13.670
Well, let's see about the insurance.

00:53:13.870 --> 00:53:15.450
We can either have it transferred or canceled.

00:53:16.330 --> 00:53:18.170
What kind of insurance do you have, Mr. Haskell?

00:53:18.350 --> 00:53:22.450
I don't know all the papers there.

00:53:22.650 --> 00:53:25.870
I don't see any.

00:53:26.530 --> 00:53:28.870
Surely you know what type of insurance you carry in the car.

00:53:29.240 --> 00:53:29.960
The name of the car.

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:35.490
company yeah but uh well if you'll just tell me the name of the company I'd be very glad to take

00:53:35.490 --> 00:53:41.580
care of all the details well did you sign the papers yet not yet well don't we're not selling

00:53:41.580 --> 00:53:45.320
the car well wait a minute Mrs. Haskell come on darling what's the matter did you change your mind

00:53:45.320 --> 00:53:57.200
yes I'm sorry I guess I have but Vera let's go got me out of a tight spot Vera but I still don't

00:53:57.200 --> 00:53:59.980
understand all this you're well in a minute I almost threw away

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:05.500
a gold mine 1850 isn't to be sneezed at the car doesn't book for as much as i thought we're not

00:54:05.500 --> 00:54:10.040
selling the car you want to keep it now wait a minute very you said yourself i wouldn't be

00:54:10.040 --> 00:54:14.060
safe until the car was in someone else's name i'd like to be free of this mess when i go that's

00:54:14.060 --> 00:54:19.310
just it roberts you're not going there's a driving at the next corner pull in there and

00:54:19.310 --> 00:54:23.380
we'll get a bite to eat and i'll explain what is this another one of your brilliant ideas

00:54:30.120 --> 00:54:31.140
Oh, may I take your order?

00:54:31.320 --> 00:54:32.760
Make mine a ham sandwich and coffee.

00:54:33.020 --> 00:54:33.620
And for you, sir?

00:54:34.030 --> 00:54:35.290
Oh, I don't care. The same.

00:54:37.820 --> 00:54:38.280
Thank you.

00:54:43.710 --> 00:54:46.230
This, Vera, I've been pretty patient so far.

00:54:46.700 --> 00:54:48.580
I've done everything you asked me to do, but no more.

00:54:48.720 --> 00:54:49.120
Shut up.

00:54:49.530 --> 00:54:50.630
You've taken Haskell's money,

00:54:51.020 --> 00:54:52.740
and you can have the door we get from selling the car,

00:54:52.920 --> 00:54:54.260
but you're not going to keep me a prisoner.

00:54:54.420 --> 00:54:56.340
It's a good thing I bought the paper. Take a look at that.

00:54:56.480 --> 00:54:57.340
Vera, I'm in no mood.

00:54:57.360 --> 00:54:57.640
Read that.

00:55:09.210 --> 00:55:11.430
No. No, I won't do it.

00:55:11.510 --> 00:55:12.090
Yes, you will.

00:55:12.350 --> 00:55:14.210
You think I'm crazy? It's impossible, I tell you.

00:55:15.400 --> 00:55:22.860
Excuse me. Blow the horn when you're through.

00:55:23.080 --> 00:55:28.560
Who could possibly get away with an act like that?

00:55:28.930 --> 00:55:29.870
It'd be wise to me in a minute.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:32.040
Don't be yellow. You look enough like him.

00:55:32.220 --> 00:55:33.580
The same coloring and the same build.

00:55:34.020 --> 00:55:35.100
See how his clothes fit you?

00:55:35.560 --> 00:55:37.500
No kidding, you almost had me fooled for a while.

00:55:37.680 --> 00:55:38.500
Oh, grow up, Vera.

00:55:38.970 --> 00:55:40.310
Don't you think a father knows his own son?

00:55:40.750 --> 00:55:41.790
And there must be other relatives.

00:55:41.890 --> 00:55:43.110
So a father won't have to know you.

00:55:43.290 --> 00:55:44.450
We'll wait till he gives up the ghost.

00:55:44.630 --> 00:55:46.250
He's an old geezer and he won't pull through.

00:55:46.760 --> 00:55:48.300
And as far as other relatives are concerned,

00:55:48.660 --> 00:55:50.480
they haven't seen you in 15 or 20 years.

00:55:52.150 --> 00:55:52.470
Eat.

00:55:52.650 --> 00:55:55.320
I'm not hungry, and I won't do it.

00:55:56.030 --> 00:55:57.270
It's not as tough as it sounds.

00:55:57.620 --> 00:55:59.160
Remember, you've got all kinds of identification.

00:55:59.480 --> 00:55:59.960
His car...

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:03.960
letters license. I could never get away with it. It's the stupidest thing I've ever heard. The old boy

00:56:03.960 --> 00:56:08.100
has scads of dough. Look in the paper there. Personal fortune assessed at over 15 million.

00:56:08.480 --> 00:56:13.040
He'll leave plenty, I tell you. Maybe he cut off his son. How do we know? It's out, Vera.

00:56:13.400 --> 00:56:18.810
I won't have anything to do with it. I think you will. Look, Vera,

00:56:19.070 --> 00:56:22.640
I'll do anything within reason, but not that. So forget it.

00:56:22.760 --> 00:56:27.840
Find yourself another stooge. You'll be fixed for the rest of your life as Charlie Haskell.

00:56:28.190 --> 00:56:29.690
You can take your inheritance and go away.

00:56:30.190 --> 00:56:33.510
No more worrying about the rent, no sweating, scheming, wondering where your next meal's coming from.

00:56:33.670 --> 00:56:34.550
Think about that, Roberts.

00:56:34.710 --> 00:56:37.230
Vera, please, you're talking too loud.

00:56:37.980 --> 00:56:39.460
Unless I'm splitting 50-50 with you.

00:56:39.640 --> 00:56:40.380
